    {
      "id": "q.tod.stairs-descend",
      "subsystem": "tod.stairs-descend",
      "question": "Which input, predicate, branch, mutations, and visible effect make up the accepted Tunnels of Doom stairs-descend transition, and how well is each part evidenced?",
      "answer": "The held FCTN+X chord appears as >8375=0A in both the positive and the held-out-negative run, so the key does not decide the outcome. VRAM >1D00 does: GPL >66A0 accepts 04 and >66A7 then requires 06, so the positive 06 continues while the negative 05 branches at >66AC to >663F and writes no filtered state. The accepted path reads >1CE8=01 and >10FE=00, increments >1CF8 00→01 at GPL >66C7, stores >1D00 06→05 at >66CB, and eight modeled frames later copies >1CF8 into >10FA 00→01 at >A798; native >08B0/>D013, >08CE/>D020, and >1D2A/>D802 perform the reads and writes. The redraw produces the DESCENDING interstitial. Broad cell names, the >1D00 enum, and >1CE8/>10FE semantics stay evidence-labeled rather than guessed."
    }
